{title: He Has Done Good To Me}
{subtitle: Psalms 13:6}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 74}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Bbmaj7] | [F] |
| [C] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]How long must [Bb]I carry worries [F]within me
With grief [C]in my heart [Dm]all the day
How long will my [Bb]enemy triumph [F]over me
Casting a [C]shadow across [Bb]my way
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Look at me [Dm]and answer, LORD [C]my God
Give light to my [Gm7]eyes before the dark takes [Bb]hold
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]But I trust in your stead[C]fast love
[Dm]My heart rejoices in [Bb]your salvation
[F]I will sing to the [C]LORD
For he has dealt [Bb]boun[C]tifully with [Dm]me [Bb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]I feared I would [Bb]sleep the sleep of death
[F]While my foes rejoiced [C]when I fell
[Dm]They said they [Bb]had overcome me
[F]But your truth is stronger [C]than my distress
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]But I trust in your stead[C]fast love
[Dm]My heart rejoices in [Bb]your salvation
[F]I will sing to the [C]LORD
For he has dealt [Bb]boun[C]tifully with [Dm]me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]No darkness can [C]hide your face from [Dm]me
Your [Bb]steadfast [C]love re[Bb]mains
You have [C]dealt bountifully with [Dm]me
In the depth of the [F]storm
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But I trust in your steadfast [C]love
[Dm]My heart rejoices in your [Bb]salvation
[F]I will sing to the [C]LORD
For he has dealt boun[Bb]ti[C]fully with me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
He [Dm]has [Bb]done good to me
He has dealt [C]bountifully with [Dm]me
{end_of_verse}

